# Common Causes for This Stripe Error

This error usually means you're trying to send raw card details directly to Stripe's API, which isn't allowed for security reasons. Here's what's likely happening:

## The Problem

You **cannot** send card details directly from your server to Stripe like this:

```javascript
// ❌ This won't work
stripe.customers.create({
  email: 'customer@example.com',
  source: {
    number: '4242424242424242',
    exp_month: 12,
    exp_year: 2025,
    cvc: '123'
  }
});
```

## The Solution

You need to tokenize card data on the **client-side** first, then send that token to your server:

### Client-side (tokenize the card):
```javascript
// Using Stripe.js
const stripe = Stripe('your_publishable_key');

const {token, error} = await stripe.createToken(cardElement);

// Send token.id to your server
fetch('/create-customer', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({ tokenId: token.id, email: 'customer@example.com' })
});
```

### Server-side (use the token):
```javascript
// Now this will work
const customer = await stripe.customers.create({
  email: req.body.email,
  source: req.body.tokenId  // The token from client-side
});
```

## Modern Approach (Recommended)

Stripe now recommends using **PaymentMethods** instead:

```javascript
// Client-side: Collect payment method
const {paymentMethod, error} = await stripe.createPaymentMethod({
  type: 'card',
  card: cardElement,
});

// Server-side: Attach to customer
const customer = await stripe.customers.create({
  email: 'customer@example.com',
  payment_method: paymentMethod.id
});
```

