# Stripe API Error: "Invalid request: must provide source or customer id"

This error typically means **you're passing raw card details instead of a Stripe token**. Stripe doesn't accept raw card data in API requests—they must be tokenized first. Here's what's likely wrong:

## The Problem

```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Raw card details won't work
const charge = await stripe.charges.create({
  amount: 1000,
  currency: 'usd',
  card: {
    number: '4242424242424242',
    exp_month: 12,
    exp_year: 2025,
    cvc: '123'
  }
});
```

## The Solution

You need to **tokenize the card first**, then use the token:

### Option 1: Using Stripe.js (Frontend)
```javascript
// Frontend - tokenize the card
const { token, error } = await stripe.createToken(card);

if (error) {
  console.log(error.message);
} else {
  // Send token to your backend
  const response = await fetch('/api/charge', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ token: token.id, amount: 1000 })
  });
}
```

### Option 2: Backend with Tokenized Source
```javascript
// Backend - use the token
const charge = await stripe.charges.create({
  amount: 1000,
  currency: 'usd',
  source: token.id  // Use the token, not raw card data
});
```

## Modern Alternative: Payment Methods API (Recommended)

```javascript
// Create a payment method (more secure)
const paymentMethod = await stripe.paymentMethods.create({
  type: 'card',
  card: {
    token: token.id  // Still use a token
  }
});

// Confirm payment with the payment method
const paymentIntent = await stripe.paymentIntents.confirm(intentId, {
  payment_method: paymentMethod.id
});
```

## Creating a Customer with Card

If you're trying to create a customer with a payment method:

```javascript
// ✅ Correct way
const customer = await stripe.customers.create({
  email: 'user@example.com',
  source: token.id  // Tokenized card
});
```

## Key Takeaways

| ❌ Don't | ✅ Do |
