| What you’re trying to do | What Stripe expects | Quick fix |
|--------------------------|--------------------|-----------|
| **Create a Customer** and give it a card in the same request | Either **no card** (just a customer record) **or** a **payment‑method token / source ID** (e.g., `source: "tok_..."` or `payment_method: "pm_..."`) | 1️⃣ Create a token (or PaymentMethod) on the client with Stripe.js / Checkout.<br>2️⃣ Pass that token/PM ID to the `source` (legacy) **or** `payment_method` field when you create the customer (or attach it later). |
| **Create a Charge / Subscription / SetupIntent** without a customer | You must send a **source** (token/PM) **or** a **customer‑id that already has a default source**. | Make sure the customer you reference already has a default payment method attached, or include `source` / `payment_method` in the request. |

The error you see (`Invalid request: must provide source or customer id.`) simply means Stripe can’t find a payment instrument to bill. Below is a deeper dive into why it happens and how to fix it, with concrete code snippets for the most common stacks.

