## 1. Understanding the “source / customer” requirement

### 1.1. Where does the rule apply?
- **Charges** (`POST /v1/charges`) – need either `source` **or** a `customer` that already has a default source.
- **Subscriptions** (`POST /v1/subscriptions`) – need a `customer` **and** a default payment method attached to that customer.
- **SetupIntents** / **PaymentIntents** – need a `payment_method` (or a token) **or** a `customer` with a saved method.

### 1.2. “Creating a customer” does **not** automatically create a card
When you call:

```http
POST https://api.stripe.com/v1/customers
```

the only required fields are `email`, `name`, `metadata`, etc. If you also want to **save a card at the same time**, you must include a **token** (legacy) or a **payment method ID** (newer API). Raw card numbers are **never** sent directly to the API—this is a security violation and will be rejected.

